fix(domain): on a runner, route calls from background fibers through the cluster

Against alchemy `packages/domain/src` at 33c10dd (2.0.0-beta.87). Apply from the repository root
with `git apply`; the text above the first `---` line is ignored.

## Problem

On a runner, `DomainCluster.layerEntities` builds the platform's namespace as
`makeNamespace(objects, { url: "", token: "", service: "" })`. `makeNamespace(...).getByName` (in
`@alchemy.run/effect-cluster`) routes a call through Effect Cluster only when `Sharding` is in the
calling fiber's context; otherwise it uses the gateway's HTTP client, here with an empty URL.

Entity handlers run with `Sharding`. Fibers that the model's Layer starts while it builds do not:
the runner bootstrap builds the entrypoint Layer before the cluster Layer exists. So any call from
such a fiber fails with `RpcClientError: HttpError: InvalidUrl (POST /rpc/)`. This covers a
stream's `list`, a view's `get` and a command's `send` alike.

## Fix

In runner mode only:

- the Layer the runner launches inside the cluster (`runner.value.host(hosted, ...)`, where the
  workflow engine is already captured) also captures the runner's `Sharding` in a `Deferred`;
- the namespace passed to `remote` gives a call whose fiber has no `Sharding` that one, waiting
  until the runner has joined. A call that already has `Sharding` goes through unchanged.

## Why it is safe

- Calls from entity handlers are unchanged (they have `Sharding`).
- A background call made before the runner has joined now waits for it instead of failing, as
  workflow calls already wait for `started`.
- No wire protocol change; one file. Callers (caller mode, through the gateway) are untouched.

An alternative is to make `makeNamespace` itself fall back to a runner-wide `Sharding` in
`@alchemy.run/effect-cluster`; this change keeps the fix inside `@alchemy.run/domain`, where the
empty URL is chosen.

## Failing case, and how it was reproduced

On a cluster (two runners and a front on Effect Cluster with PostgreSQL 17, on a single-node Docker
swarm on one workstation), a model whose Layer forks a poller (`Effect.forkScoped`) that reads another
model's fact stream and sends a command for each fact. Before the change every read from the poller
failed with `InvalidUrl`: the fact was published and never consumed, and a run waiting for it never
concluded. After it, the poller consumed the fact, and the run completed, across a runner restart
and across a `pg_dump` and restore into a fresh stack.

## Where it ran

- On a cluster: the case above, in several runs.
- In process: nothing. Reproducing it needs the runner bootstrap.

## Depends on

Nothing. No hunk overlaps any other patch here.
